      "stem": "To plot the line $y = -x + 4$, which table of values is correct?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$x = 0, y = 4$; $x = 2, y = 6$; $x = 4, y = 8$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$x = 0, y = 4$; $x = 2, y = 2$; $x = 4, y = 0$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$x = 0, y = 0$; $x = 2, y = 2$; $x = 4, y = 4$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$x = 0, y = -4$; $x = 2, y = -2$; $x = 4, y = 0$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "For $y = -x + 4$: when $x = 0$, $y = 4$; when $x = 2$, $y = -2 + 4 = 2$; when $x = 4$, $y = -4 + 4 = 0$."
